  "summary": "The Danish art of cozy conviviality: candlelight, wool socks, warm drinks and contented togetherness through dark winters.",
  "description": "Hygge — a Danish/Norwegian concept of cozy, well-being-centered contentment — shapes Nordic interiors (candle density, sheepskins, warm wood, firelight) and social rituals (coffee, gatherings, low light). The 2016 book boom exported it globally as a lifestyle brand, joining lagom and friluftsliv in the Nordic wellness lexicon. As an aesthetic it means warm-pool lighting, natural textures and gentle, uncluttered comfort.",
